Ported the Solend flash‑loan path to production quality, tightened Port Finance handling, and added a Jet Protocol provider scaffold.

  Key changes

  - crates/flash-loan-providers/src/solend/mod.rs (+ solend/instructions.rs) now own the full devnet WSOL configuration, instruction builders, fee math, and regression tests. Borrow/
  repay plans are produced and executor logging (crates/executor-service/src/execution_engine.rs:809-833) captures every successful plan with instruction counts.
  - crates/flash-loan-providers/src/port_finance/mod.rs quotes Port but intentionally returns a descriptive error because Port’s token-lending program still mandates a CPI receiver.
  Validation tests ensure we’ll catch it once a receiver program exists.
  - New crates/flash-loan-providers/src/jet/mod.rs mirrors that pattern for Jet: it registers when the env supplies reserve metadata, quotes with a placeholder 35 bps fee, and surfaces
  the same “receiver required” error until we add that component. Tests verify the config guardrails.
  - Executor aggregator registers Jet alongside Marginfi, Solend, and Port, so configuration already accepts jetprotocol should you enable it by providing the env keys.

  Verification

  - cargo test -p flash-loan-providers
  - cargo check -p executor-service

  What you need to configure

  1. Solend – the WSOL host-fee account is already synced; just export before running:

     export SOLEND_WSOL_HOST_FEE_ACCOUNT=AJVS4MHtdmwnKAkKbuX7FUKVwhuEM1woVRVctS4Gi33S
     (Re-run spl-token sync-native --fee-payer ~/.config/solana/id.json --address AJVS4MHtdmwnKAkKbuX7FUKVwhuEM1woVRVctS4Gi33S whenever you top it up.)
  2. Port Finance – to unlock real execution, we still need to build/deploy a flash-loan receiver program and then we can wire its program id into the plan builder.
  3. Jet Protocol – set the env vars so registration succeeds and point to the shared receiver program:

     export JET_LENDING_MARKET=<pubkey>
     export JET_RESERVE=<pubkey>
     export JET_RESERVE_LIQUIDITY_SUPPLY=<pubkey>
     export JET_FEE_RECEIVER=<pubkey>
     # optional override if you have it:
     # export JET_MARKET_AUTHORITY=<pubkey>
     Once those are in place you’ll at least receive Jet quotes. Deploy the receiver program (see `crates/flash-loan-receiver/`) and update `FLASH_LOAN_RECEIVER_PROGRAM_ID` so Jet plans include the CPI hand-off.

  When you want to continue:

  - Capture a devnet run to confirm Solend bundles (watch for flash_loan_plan_ready provider=solend … and the borrow/repay instructions).
  - Build & deploy the receiver contract (see `docs/operations/FLASH_LOAN_RECEIVER_PROGRAM.md`), update `FLASH_LOAN_RECEIVER_PROGRAM_ID`, and rerun the executor to exercise Port/Jet plans end-to-end.
